From 637deced104a7d7e1aed83ff4e718303e6ee5f4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:18:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] fix(trace): fill only grey cracks, not drawn white lines
 (ADR-392)

Operator change: with Fill tiny holes on, the tracer still closes
hairline slivers that thresholding cut into solid ink, but only when
every pixel of the sliver was nearer the cut than the paper level in the
image before the cut (luma - threshold <= paper - luma, paper = median
luma of the mask's paper pixels). A white line the artist drew has pixels
at paper level, so it now stays open. Masks that carry no luma before the
cut (alpha masks, two-sided brightness bands) keep the shape tests only.
The checkbox still turns filling on or off and the preset defaults are
unchanged. Slivers are now grouped the way the outline walker traces
them: paper pixels that touch at a corner belong to one sliver where the
walker joins paper there, so a diagonal white line is judged whole.

Measured on the dragon (1254 px) with the whole package applied: of the
1,461 slivers that pass the shape tests in Line Art, 718 grey ones still
fill and 743 bright ones stay open (Smooth: 1,021 of 2,154 fill). At the
old speck sizes, leaving them open adds 730 Line Art and 1,158 Smooth
outlines compared with filling them all; in the crops checked they are
white gaps between hatch strokes. On the Arch House logo every sliver is grey (at most 39
luma above the cut), so filling is unchanged there: 6 slivers in Line Art
and 35 in Smooth.

TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx's tiny-hole test assumed pure
white slits fill; the next commit adapts it, so land the two together.

